      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T20:44:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, I\u0027m not limiting when deapexer modules are created anymore (as opposed to some earlier iterations on these CLs). So in unbundled builds they\u0027re still created as usual, but instead carry invalidReasons.\n\nThat means this error exactly corresponds to the one before this CL, and only triggers if there for some reason isn\u0027t a deapexer module at all. Before https://r.android.com/1829372 it was argued to be an internal error, and that\u0027s probably still true, but I don\u0027t think it\u0027s safe to carry over that argument when moving it to a generic function like this.\n\nThat said, if it truly is an internal error I think it would also make sense to go the other way and change this to a panic and document that this function assumes it will find at least one deapexer module (invalid or not).",
      "parentUuid": "9716e5d4_5c8290f5",
      "revId": "4018b50ac2082677be51022b577ab29602718d0a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
